<h3 id="how-our-jwt-flow-works" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight"><span>How Our JWT Flow Works</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#how-our-jwt-flow-works" aria-label="Link to How Our JWT Flow Works"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h3>
<p>To understand how JWT fits into our Go authentication system, let&#x27;s walk through the flow of a user logging in and accessing protected routes:</p>
<ol>
<li>
<p>When a user successfully authenticates, our Go service:</p>
<ul>
<li>Validates credentials against Neon Postgres</li>
<li>Creates JWT with appropriate claims and expiration</li>
<li>Signs the token with a secret key</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>
<p>The client:</p>
<ul>
<li>Stores the JWT (typically in <code>localStorage</code> or a secure cookie)</li>
<li>Includes the token in the <code>Authorization</code> header for subsequent requests</li>
</ul>
<figure class="code-block group/code-block relative flex flex-col [&amp;_pre]:min-w-full rounded-none border border-gray-new-80 dark:border-gray-new-20 [&amp;&gt;pre]:my-0 [&amp;&gt;pre]:rounded-none [&amp;&gt;pre]:bg-white! [&amp;&gt;pre]:py-4 [&amp;&gt;pre]:dark:bg-black-pure!" data-has-filename="false" data-line-numbers="false"><pre class="shiki css-variables" style="background-color:var(--shiki-background);color:var(--shiki-foreground)" tabindex="0" data-language="text"><code class="grid"><span class="line" data-line="1"><span>Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1Ni...</span></span></code></pre><button class="invisible absolute right-4 border border-gray-new-80 bg-white p-1.5 text-gray-new-40 opacity-0 transition-[background-color,opacity,visibility] duration-200 group-hover/code-block:visible group-hover/code-block:opacity-100 hover:bg-gray-new-90 dark:border-gray-new-20 dark:bg-black-pure dark:text-gray-new-60 dark:hover:bg-gray-new-8 lg:visible lg:opacity-100 top-[min(1rem,calc(50%-.8175rem))]" type="button" aria-label="Copy"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 16 16" class="h-3.5 w-3.5 text-current"><rect width="8.995" height="9.002" x="5.939" y="5.935" stroke="currentColor" rx="1"></rect><path fill="currentColor" fill-rule="evenodd" d="M2.434.935a1.5 1.5 0 0 0-1.5 1.5v7.001a1.5 1.5 0 0 0 1.5 1.5h1.499a.5.5 0 0 0 0-1h-1.5a.5.5 0 0 1-.5-.5V2.435a.5.5 0 0 1 .5-.5h6.995a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v1.5a.5.5 0 1 0 1 0v-1.5a1.5 1.5 0 0 0-1.5-1.5z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path></svg></button></figure>
</li>
<li>
<p>Our middleware:</p>
<ul>
<li>Extracts the JWT from the request header</li>
<li>Validates the signature using our secret key</li>
<li>Checks that the token hasn&#x27;t expired</li>
<li>Extracts the user identity from claims</li>
<li>Adds the user ID to the request context</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>
<p>Since the token contains all necessary user information, our server can authenticate requests without maintaining session state or additional database queries.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p>The security of this system relies on keeping the signing key secret and using short-lived access tokens. If a token is compromised, it&#x27;s only valid for a limited time, reducing the risk of unauthorized access.</p>
<h2 id="create-a-neon-project" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter"><span>Create a Neon project</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#create-a-neon-project" aria-label="Link to Create a Neon project"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h2>
<p>First, let&#x27;s create a Neon project to store our authentication data.</p>
<ol>
<li>Navigate to the <a class="group inline" href="https://console.neon.tech/app/projects" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Neon Console<span class="whitespace-nowrap no-underline"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="ml-1 inline-block size-3.5! shrink-0 align-[-0.125em]"><path fill="currentColor" d="M0 0h14v14H0z" opacity="0.2"></path><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" d="M9.915 8.885V4.08H5.11M9.625 4.375 4.083 9.917"></path></svg></span></a> and click New Project.</li>
<li>Give your project a name, such as &quot;auth-system&quot;.</li>
<li>Choose your preferred region.</li>
<li>Click Create Project.</li>
</ol>
<p>Once your project is created, you&#x27;ll receive a connection string that looks like this:</p>
<figure class="code-block group/code-block relative flex flex-col [&amp;_pre]:min-w-full rounded-none border border-gray-new-80 dark:border-gray-new-20 [&amp;&gt;pre]:my-0 [&amp;&gt;pre]:rounded-none [&amp;&gt;pre]:bg-white! [&amp;&gt;pre]:py-4 [&amp;&gt;pre]:dark:bg-black-pure!" data-has-filename="false" data-line-numbers="false"><pre class="shiki css-variables" style="background-color:var(--shiki-background);color:var(--shiki-foreground)" tabindex="0" data-language="text"><code class="grid"><span class="line" data-line="1"><span>postgres://[user]:[password]@[hostname]/[dbname]?sslmode=require&amp;channel_binding=require</span></span></code></pre><button class="invisible absolute right-4 border border-gray-new-80 bg-white p-1.5 text-gray-new-40 opacity-0 transition-[background-color,opacity,visibility] duration-200 group-hover/code-block:visible group-hover/code-block:opacity-100 hover:bg-gray-new-90 dark:border-gray-new-20 dark:bg-black-pure dark:text-gray-new-60 dark:hover:bg-gray-new-8 lg:visible lg:opacity-100 top-[min(1rem,calc(50%-.8175rem))]" type="button" aria-label="Copy"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 16 16" class="h-3.5 w-3.5 text-current"><rect width="8.995" height="9.002" x="5.939" y="5.935" stroke="currentColor" rx="1"></rect><path fill="currentColor" fill-rule="evenodd" d="M2.434.935a1.5 1.5 0 0 0-1.5 1.5v7.001a1.5 1.5 0 0 0 1.5 1.5h1.499a.5.5 0 0 0 0-1h-1.5a.5.5 0 0 1-.5-.5V2.435a.5.5 0 0 1 .5-.5h6.995a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v1.5a.5.5 0 1 0 1 0v-1.5a1.5 1.5 0 0 0-1.5-1.5z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path></svg></button></figure>
<p>Save this connection string, you&#x27;ll need it to connect your Go application to the Neon database.</p>
<h2 id="set-up-the-database-schema" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter"><span>Set up the database schema</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#set-up-the-database-schema" aria-label="Link to Set up the database schema"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h2>
<p>Now we&#x27;ll create a database schema that securely stores user information and authentication tokens. Connect to your Neon database and run the following SQL to create the necessary tables:</p>
<figure class="code-block group/code-block relative flex flex-col [&amp;_pre]:min-w-full rounded-none border border-gray-new-80 dark:border-gray-new-20 [&amp;&gt;pre]:my-0 [&amp;&gt;pre]:rounded-none [&amp;&gt;pre]:bg-white! [&amp;&gt;pre]:py-4 [&amp;&gt;pre]:dark:bg-black-pure!" data-has-filename="false" data-line-numbers="false"><pre class="shiki css-variables" style="background-color:var(--shiki-background);color:var(--shiki-foreground)" tabindex="0" data-language="sql"><code class="grid"><span class="line" data-line="1"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-comment)">-- Create users table</span></span>
<span class="line" data-line="2"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">CREATE</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)"> TABLE</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-function)"> users</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)"> (</span></span>
<span class="line" data-line="3"><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)">    id UUID </span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">PRIMARY KEY</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)"> DEFAULT</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)"> gen_random_uuid(),</span></span>
<span class="line" data-line="4"><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)">    email </span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">VARCHAR</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)">(</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-constant)">255</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)">) </span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">UNIQUE</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)"> NOT NULL</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)">,</span></span>
<span class="line" data-line="5"><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)">    username </span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">VARCHAR</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)">(</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-constant)">50</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)">) </span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">UNIQUE</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)"> NOT NULL</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)">,</span></span>
