<p>Bcrypt is used for password hashing because:</p>
<ol>
<li>It&#x27;s slow by design, making brute-force attacks impractical</li>
<li>It automatically includes a salt to protect against rainbow table attacks</li>
<li>It has an adjustable cost factor to increase security as hardware gets faster</li>
<li>It&#x27;s a one-way function that can&#x27;t be reversed to obtain the original password</li>
</ol>
<p>When a user registers, we&#x27;ll hash their password before storing it. When they log in, we&#x27;ll compare their provided password against the stored hash.</p>
